{
  "summary": "Reported: James O'Connor (Warehouse Supervisor, Operations, user_id 8) says his desktop has no network and floor 2 printer BL-PR-FL2 is down. Checked: account active, no lockout or block. BL-DT-0108 (wired desktop, Win11) shows online=false, last check-in 2026-10-11 01:02 UTC, no warnings, disk fine. BL-PR-FL2 shows online=false, last check-in 2026-10-10 22:02 UTC, no warnings. Two wired devices dropped within about 3 hours of each other. That points to a possible network fault (switch, port, or floor-2 segment) rather than two separate device faults. No KB covers a wired desktop with no network. KB-014's escalate-when (office network down for several people) may apply, and KB-022's escalate-when applies if the printer stays offline after a power cycle with no error shown. User was asked to check the desktop cable and link light and restart, to have someone check the printer screen and power-cycle it, and to report whether colleagues nearby are affected. Still needed: check the switch/ports serving the desktop and BL-PR-FL2, confirm scope (how many others on the floor are affected), and re-prioritize to P1 if it is widespread.",
  "reason": "Two wired devices offline around the same time suggests a network fault. No KB for wired desktop connectivity, and I can't fix it with my tools."
}
